# AI-PLC Adaptive Workflow

## When to Use (RUL_plc_adaptive §0)

"Record broadly, keep procedures lean": decide separately whether a Layer (record) is needed and which safeguards apply. One-off / generic / personal work gets no Layer; work you will revisit or that spans sessions gets a Layer with ○/× done criteria; work needing repository- or org-specific context gets Context collection; decision material for others gets an independent review per task; irreversible actions by the AI (publish, send, core rules/skills, external DB, delete, money) need human approval first. If the depth suggested here differs from the criteria below, the criteria win and the reason goes in `workflow_depth_reason`.

## Workflow Depth Detection

| Depth | Criteria | Pipeline Behavior | Verification |
|-------|----------|-------------------|-------------|
| Simple | Single domain, 1-2 tasks, known pattern | Stage 1→4 direct (Stage 3 only when the conditions below apply) | L1 only |
| Standard | Multiple tasks, no Sub-Layer needed | Stage 1→2→4 (Stage 3 only when the conditions below apply) | L1+L2 |
| Complex | Recursive decomposition needed, large scale | All 4 stages + Sub-Layer recursion | L1+L2+L3+NFR |

## Mode Detection

| Mode | Condition | Pipeline |
|------|-----------|----------|
| Direct | One-time execution | Stage 1-4, complete |
| Platform Builder | Building reusable system | Stage 1-4 + Production Skill generation |

## Next Action Routing

| Current State | Next Action |
|---------------|-------------|
| Stage 1 complete | → Stage 2 (Inception) |
| Stage 2 complete | backlog `construction.required: true` → Stage 3 (Construction); false → Stage 4 (Operation) |
| Stage 3 complete | → Stage 4 (Operation) |
| Task complete (more remain) | → Next executable task |
| All tasks complete (Direct) | → Pipeline end |
| All tasks complete (Platform Builder) | → Production Skill generation |

## Stage 3 (Construction) is skipped by default

Run Stage 3 (Agent definitions) only when: complex depth, platform_builder mode, `construction_mode: always` in intent.yaml, a task with `delegable: true`, or an implementation/coding task with more than 5 steps. Whoever writes the backlog records the decision in the top-level `construction` (required / reason / tasks). Without Stage 3, Operation executes from the backlog (description, acceptance_criteria, guardrails, decisions) and Context. See RUL_plc_adaptive §6.
